&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Coursera + Udemy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coursera and Udemy are now one company, bringing together two mission-driven brands to create the world’s most powerful platform for turning learning into progress. Together, we help more than 300 million learners and 12,000+ enterprise customers build the skills they need for a world being reshaped by AI. Read more about the combined company by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.coursera.org/coursera-and-udemy-are-now-one-company-creating-the-worlds-most-comprehensive-skills-platform/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us now?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is transforming how people learn, work, and grow, and the need for new skills has never been greater. Coursera brings trusted content and credentials from leading university and industry partners, while Udemy brings a dynamic skills marketplace and global network of real-world experts. By combining these strengths, we can connect more people and organizations to the skills they need, when they need them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape what comes next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our team, you’ll have the opportunity to reshape how the world learns and applies skills—and help millions of people participate in the new economy. Bring your ideas, expertise, and perspective to meaningful work that can make a difference at global scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Coursera + Udemy lets you choose the best way to work, whether it’s from home, an office, or a collaboration space. We’re a globally distributed team that comes together intentionally for collaboration, complex problem-solving, and key milestones — creating opportunities for teams to come together. If you’re ready to make a global impact, help scale unique products across Coursera + Udemy, and grow your career, apply below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About this role:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Strategy and Operations team at Coursera partners with all areas of the marketing organization and the enterprise sales team to drive revenue, design and execute marketing strategies, and lead internal processes to enhance productivity, leverage, and efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Creative Operations Program Manager, you will be the primary architect of the systems and processes that power Coursera’s creative output. You will manage the complex interplay of creative demand from marketing and product stakeholders, the execution capacity of our internal creative teams, and the strategic support of our external agency partners. Your goal is to establish a best-in-class operational model that ensures high-quality, distinctive creative work is delivered on budget and on time through effective cross-functional governance and resource optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About your skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt; — You build trust across marketing, product, and creative teams, and know how to align competing priorities into a single shared roadmap. You&#39;ll be the connective tissue between stakeholders and the creative teams delivering their work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinking&lt;/strong&gt; — You see workflows end-to-end, not just in pieces. You&#39;ll design and refine the processes — from intake to final delivery — that keep creative work moving smoothly across internal teams and external agency partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resourcefulness&lt;/strong&gt; — You know how to make the most of limited capacity, balancing internal bandwidth against agency support to keep projects on track without sacrificing quality or blowing the budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Communication&lt;/strong&gt; — You translate operational detail and performance metrics into clear, compelling updates — whether you&#39;re briefing a creative team or reporting up to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, implement, and audit end-to-end creative workflows—from unified intake and brief grooming to final delivery—ensuring streamlined handoffs between marketing, product, and creative teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program/Project Leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead complex, cross-functional creative initiatives from intake through delivery, driving timelines, dependency management, stakeholder alignment, risk mitigation, and launch readiness across marketing, product, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Drive adoption of new workflows, tools, and operating models through documentation, training, and stakeholder enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource &amp;amp; Agency Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead quarterly and weekly resource planning, balancing internal team bandwidth with a varied roster of external agencies to ensure optimal workload distribution and cost efficiency. Proactively identify capacity constraints and recommend prioritization, staffing, or agency engagement strategies to mitigate delivery risks and maintain execution quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrate cross-functional interlocks and steering meetings to align marketing/product objectives with creative capabilities, effectively communicating project tradeoffs and resource availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MarTech Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the functional lead for the creative technology stack (e.g., Asana, DAM systems), integrating operational efficiencies into the ticketing and asset management processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish KPI frameworks and dashboards to track creative throughput, quality, and business impact, providing regular strategic updates to senior management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Relations:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage external agency contracts, renewals, and onboarding in partnership with Procurement and Legal, ensuring all partners adhere to Coursera’s brand and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a Creative Producer, Program Manager, or Project Manager working directly with high-volume creative teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing resource planning, budget mitigation, and external agency relationships within a marketing or product organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level proficiency in project management tools (e.g., Asana, Jira, or Airtable) and experience building automated workflows within these systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven history of leading cross-functional collaboration and developing clear project roadmaps for complex, omni-channel campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Objective history of establishing operational efficiencies that reduced time-to-market or production costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced program management skills with a track record of managing competing deliverables for both B2C and B2B SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Agile methodologies or experience serving as a Scrum Master for creative sprints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills to assess operational bottlenecks and develop data-driven solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills with the ability to influence senior leadership and translate technical requirements into creative briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Digital Asset Management (DAM) implementation and creative production software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Compensation&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Coursera, we offer competitive, zone-based pay aligned to your location, experience, and role level. Our total rewards package goes beyond salary, with comprehensive health and wellness benefits, bonus and RSU equity programs, and global perks designed to help you grow and thrive wherever you are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is only available for hire in Zone 3 and Zone 4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;US Zone 3: $114,000-$143,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;US Zone 4: $106,000-$133,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;US Pay Zones:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z1: Bay Area (within 75 miles)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z2: NYC and Seattle Metro (within 75 miles)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z3: CA, WA, NY, NJ, CO, CT, DC, GA, IL, MA, MD, OR, RI, TX, VA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z4: AK, AZ, DE, FL, HI, ID, IN, IA, KS, KY, MI, MN, MO, MT, NC, NV, NH, OH, OK, PA, SC, TN, UT, VT, WI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Posting Date&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Posting Date: September 10, 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Application Window:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We anticipate the application window will be open until September 24, 2026. Based on business needs, this opportunity may remain posted beyond or closed before the anticipated application window.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information about how Coursera collects and uses your personal information, please see our &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.clinchtalent.com/1d7f2c0f91ebf75d580f56447fa54859/2acb24eb91f1e23b90ac9e9285de5aaf/Coursera%20and%20Udemy%20Global%20Applicant%20Privacy%20Notice.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Coursera + Udemy Global Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect against recruitment fraud, Coursera + Udemy recruiters only communicate via official coursera.org/udemy.com email addresses and never through personal accounts. We do not accept resumes via email or social media; please submit all applications directly through our careers page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you encounter suspicious recruitment activity, please report it via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/Mb8UktwuaJAukb3H7&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Submission Form.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coursera is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building a welcoming and inclusive workplace. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to legally protected characteristics and provide reasonable accommodations upon request at recruiting@coursera.org.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
